# Repository Language

Repository-authored prose must be written in English. This applies to documentation, ADRs, plans,
notes, memos, harnesses, code comments, and test names.

The language used in conversation does not change the repository language. A request for a
Japanese or other non-English report authorizes a chat response in that language, not a committed
repository artifact in that language. Only an explicit request to change the repository language
policy can change this boundary.

Non-English text is allowed only when the artifact requires the original text, such as localization
documentation, translation data or fixtures, customer-visible localized copy, a relevant quotation,
or Unicode and locale test data. Explain an exception next to the affected text.

Before finishing prose work, review the files you touched for non-English prose.

Do not relabel ordinary prose as localization to make it pass. Translate the prose or document the
narrow, genuine exception.
